# DLV-4: accepted findings, with the reason. An open finding that everyone has
# learned to scroll past is worse than a recorded decision.

# AVD-GCP-0029 / AVD-GCP-0076 — VPC flow logs disabled on the subnet.
#
# Accepted. The only traffic that crosses this VPC is Cloud Run reaching
# Memorystore on TCP 6379, from one subnet, allowed by one firewall rule
# (modules/networking). There is no lateral movement to detect between two
# resources, and flow logs on a subnet carrying one flow bill for volume that
# answers no question anyone will ask. The edge is where the traffic worth
# logging is, and OPS-2 turned that on.
#
# Revisit if the VPC ever carries a second workload.
AVD-GCP-0029
AVD-GCP-0076
